    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 3,
        "sourceEnd": 59,
        "text": "Hi Lisa, how was your trip to the city transport museum?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "cf1ad5025f55af352d17cdd08c3e28d93699779f91c6cd66d22b0340d5e82934",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 63,
        "sourceEnd": 162,
        "text": "It was really interesting, Tom. I learned a lot about how people moved around the city in the past.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "0ac39b29dbee1bc33a16f5d20205f9c91eea74ebe97eb38a8b7b358196e9081d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 166,
        "sourceEnd": 197,
        "text": "Oh yeah? What did you find out?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "3d1e07ab2fd4671788493ee5ce67edf41200ce8eaee2eee3a96d8046bc89d90d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 201,
        "sourceEnd": 393,
        "text": "Well, they had this big chart showing the number of bus passengers from 1990 to 2020. In 1990, about 2 million people used the bus every day. But by 2020, that number had dropped to 1 million.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "7be25ef94b76203b905e66c35026aa94fa07f1aa1073c7d32902691149310d73",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 397,
        "sourceEnd": 410,
        "text": "So it halved?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "917bd34888a49b968242014782ef5d5cda8f58ee1afac435bf914ae6773fe319",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 414,
        "sourceEnd": 607,
        "text": "Exactly. The bus passenger number halved over those 30 years. But the subway passenger number more than tripled. In 1990, only 500,000 people used the subway daily. By 2020, it was 1.8 million.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "3b6509a5eaec99d42b8d1a705839c4f448e500da199c7c920ae8ba70b28e41b5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 611,
        "sourceEnd": 666,
        "text": "That's a huge increase. Why do you think that happened?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "501890b28e5595d4180e8bd6877fe2f0a71b10437f12b524341062dd62f43600",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 670,
        "sourceEnd": 834,
        "text": "The museum guide said the subway became faster and more reliable. Also, the city built many new subway lines. The bus system didn't change much, so people switched.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "5d5f08df23a9255c46b65317bafff6f810785c475fe1636590ed712cedf6c22d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 838,
        "sourceEnd": 876,
        "text": "Did they show anything about bicycles?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "17545eebae335ef22e734e69781d24cab70ce68eaeca45919753cdc8d27f2bb5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 880,
        "sourceEnd": 1078,
        "text": "Yes, they had a chart for bicycle use too. In 1990, about 10% of commuters cycled to work. But in 2020, it was only 3%. The guide said safety concerns and longer distances made cycling less popular.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "45424f3c5001dd1039919a46f0fa6bc6cbd4d1d2da93c6034e4a7de4272fc00d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1082,
        "sourceEnd": 1133,
        "text": "That's a shame. Bikes are good for the environment.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "64520b0bf5fc58a6b6cdea32298c3d59f2cd9dfb5cbc965e201682f7cc1b50ed",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1137,
        "sourceEnd": 1307,
        "text": "I agree. But now there are shared bikes. The museum had a small section about them. Shared bikes started in 2016, and by 2020, there were 50,000 shared bikes in the city.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "eae74a9b5d9803eebe4ccc6aff0d93957f0c04190ebc1dbdee32db608db267f6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1311,
        "sourceEnd": 1355,
        "text": "Wow, that's a lot. Do people use them often?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "83f9c94c4e49f0aef5718d7d71f70bf19b1c12d03dddbe93fb0386bc4fe18d02",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1359,
        "sourceEnd": 1507,
        "text": "The chart showed that each shared bike is used about 4 times a day on average. That's much more than private bikes, which are used maybe once a day.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "b7342e8df068c4ddba5a833922b24a946c9937c75c67b0076819a5675526ee26",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1511,
        "sourceEnd": 1546,
        "text": "So shared bikes are more efficient?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "dee8d9a9e3cd4b368ef1a36dd1b86ee02271d44f486fda24aa60d0187e6b36fb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1550,
        "sourceEnd": 1718,
        "text": "Yes, in terms of usage. But the museum also said that shared bikes need more maintenance. The city spends twice as much on maintaining shared bikes as on private bikes.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "5ff0aadd0f0507b306cb6afe05e3e743ebe2caee4800f73341598a3855579b39",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1722,
        "sourceEnd": 1765,
        "text": "Interesting. So what's the overall picture?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "3b18ce22d1e7bb34013b29a560bab56776263e674957bd3de438e7c90cdda992",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1769,
        "sourceEnd": 1974,
        "text": "Well, public transport, especially the subway, has grown a lot. Bus use has gone down. Cycling has decreased, but shared bikes are a new option. The city is definitely moving towards more public transport.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "824a19924536f092e9b7b2499a14ddb77a08d15966bf7d86ba6fa04f5aa58368",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1978,
        "sourceEnd": 2020,
        "text": "Thanks, Lisa. That was really informative.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "8411464d8f9bc1d29ddc65b8e75deeb48e0d44a064dca1f63e1d93815b252962",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
